-- title:
--   Two branches at supersingular points of the X₁(Mp) model
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime and $M$ a non-zero natural number with $5 \le M$ and $p \nmid M$; let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero that is a cyclotomic extension of $\mathbb{Q}$ of order $p$, and $\zeta \in L$ a primitive $p$-th root of unity. Let $K$ be an intermediate field of $L \subseteq \mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,L$ equal to [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange L (ModularCurve.x1FunctionField (M * p))`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103), i.e. the $L$-subfield generated by the image of the intermediate field `x1FunctionField (M * p)` of $\mathbb{Q} \subseteq \mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,\mathbb{Q}$ under the coefficientwise map induced by $\mathbb{Q} \to L$. Let $A$ be a discrete valuation domain with fraction field $L$ such that $p$ lies in the maximal ideal of $A$ and $\zeta$ lies in the image of $A$, with an $A$-algebra structure on $K$ compatible with $L$, and let $\varpi$ generate the maximal ideal of $A$. Let $j \in K$ be non-zero with underlying Laurent series the image of [`ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L157) $= q^{-1}\cdot j_{\mathrm{num}}$ under the coefficient embedding. Write $X =$ [`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel A K j`](def/AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel.html#L236), the pushout of the two maps from the Spec of the middle chart algebra to $X_{\mathrm{fin}} = \operatorname{Spec} A_{\mathrm{fin}}$ and $X_\infty$, where $A_{\mathrm{fin}} =$ `chartAlgFin` is the subalgebra of elements of $K$ integral over $A[j]$, with structure morphism `toBase` to $\operatorname{Spec} A$. Let $z \in X$ and let $\varpi_z$ be the germ at $z$ of the image of $\varpi$ under $A \to \Gamma(X)$, and assume $\varpi_z$ lies in the maximal ideal of the stalk $\mathcal{O}_{X,z}$. Assume $z$ is the image under `ιFin` of a point $y$ of $X_{\mathrm{fin}}$ such that for every algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $p$ and every ring homomorphism $\varphi : A_{\mathrm{fin}} \to \Omega$ with kernel the prime of $y$, the value $\varphi(j)$ lies in [`ModularCurve.ssJSet p Ω`](def/ModularCurve_SupersingularModuli.html#L7), that is: every elliptic Weierstrass curve over $\Omega$ with $j$-invariant $\varphi(j)$ has no non-zero point $P$ with $p \cdot P = 0$. Then the set of minimal primes of the ideal $\varpi_z \mathcal{O}_{X,z}$ is not a subsingleton, i.e. it contains at least two distinct members.
--
--   This is the statement that at a supersingular point of the special fibre of the two-chart integral model of $X_1(Mp)$ over a discrete valuation ring containing $\zeta_p$ above $p$, at least two algebraic branches of the special fibre pass through the point, with no regularity or singularity hypothesis imposed at $z$. It feeds the local analysis of the special fibre at such points, in particular the statements about non-regularity of the fibre stalk and the comparison of the completed local ring with that of a crossing model.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_XOneP_not_subsingleton_minimalPrimes_span_germ_of_mem_ssJSet_twoChartIntegralModel_x1_mul.lean

